-----------
 ssh-theme
-----------

Sync macOS appearance to tmux and Neovim on a Linux SSH server.

The Mac needs a ~/.local/bin/term-theme command that applies its local theme,
and passwordless SSH access to the server. The server needs tmux, nvim, and
GNU timeout. Supply these palettes yourself:

    ~/.config/terminal-style/light/theme.tmux
    ~/.config/terminal-style/dark/theme.tmux
    ~/.config/nvim/colors/reference.lua

The Neovim colorscheme must support both backgrounds. Change "reference" in
nvim/lua/terminal_theme.lua if yours has another name.

On the server, from the repo root:

```sh
mkdir -p "$HOME/.local/bin" "$HOME/.config/nvim/lua"
install -m 755 examples/ssh-theme/remote-term-theme.sh "$HOME/.local/bin/term-theme"
install -m 644 examples/ssh-theme/nvim/lua/terminal_theme.lua "$HOME/.config/nvim/lua/terminal_theme.lua"
install -m 755 examples/ssh-theme/nvim/refresh-theme.sh "$HOME/.config/nvim/refresh-theme.sh"
```

Add to ~/.config/nvim/init.lua, replacing the old theme callback:

```lua
require("terminal_theme").setup()
```

Restart existing editors after installing. The refresh script uses
Neovim's default sockets under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (or /run/user/$(id -u)); adjust
it if you use custom --listen paths.

On the Mac, from the repo root:

```sh
mkdir -p "$HOME/.local/bin"
install -m 755 examples/ssh-theme/sync-theme.sh "$HOME/.local/bin/sync-theme"
THEME_SSH_HOST=your-server macnotify "$HOME/.local/bin/sync-theme"
```

For login startup, use ../macnotify.plist with sync-theme as the command and
THEME_SSH_HOST in EnvironmentVariables. See ../../README for loading the agent.
